{
    "name": "pdfnative-mcp",
    "version": "1.6.0",
    "description": "Model Context Protocol (MCP) server (27 tools, MCP 2026-07-28 with automatic 2025-era fallback) bridging the zero-dependency pdfnative v1.7 library — generate PDFs (PDF/A-1b/2b/2u/3b with embedded fonts and conformance diagnostics) with bookmarks/outline, page labels & viewer preferences, print production (page boxes, bleed, printer's marks, /Trapped, ICC output intent), render native vector charts v2 (bar / stacked / line / area / scatter / pie / donut, dual axis, log & time scales), add markup annotations, merge / split / extract pages, update document metadata, validate PDF/UA structure, embed barcodes & QR codes, sign (constant-time node:crypto, RSA-SHA256/384/512 / ECDSA P-256) and **verify** PAdES documents through the full long-term-validation ladder (B-B / B-T / B-LT / B-LTA: RFC 3161 timestamps, /DSS with OCSP & CRL, document timestamps), decrypt & re-encrypt (RC4 / AES-128 / AES-256), fill & flatten AcroForms, render 24 scripts including colour emoji and math symbols, build smart tables and AcroForms, embed images, embed files (Factur-X / ZUGFeRD PDF/A-3), extract Unicode text with positioned runs, inspect existing PDFs, expose generated PDFs as MCP resources, and draft human-in-the-loop GitHub issues under an AI-governance contract — no outbound network by default — from any MCP-compatible AI client (Claude, Cursor, ChatGPT, Continue, Zed, Windsurf, Cline, Roo Code, …).",
